  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Ser»",
     "texto": [
      "Use **ser** to say where you're from (**Sou de Madrid**), your profession (**Sou professora**) and characteristics you present as your own (**O Pedro é alto**).",
      "These are frequent uses, not an absolute rule of «permanent»: the verb also depends on the meaning and on the expression."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Estar»",
     "texto": [
      "Use **estar** for where you are (**Estou em casa**), how you feel (**Estou cansado**) and the current state of something (**A loja está aberta**).",
      "**Ser** and **estar** can change the meaning: **O Miguel é simpático** talks about his character; **Hoje está simpático** describes how he comes across today. Also memorise common expressions such as **estar bem** and **estar com fome**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Watch out for the same adjective",
     "texto": [
      "**O Miguel é simpático** (Miguel is nice: his character).",
      "**Hoje o Miguel está simpático** (today Miguel is in a good mood). Same adjective, different meaning."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
